WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
In 1859, Charles Darwin argued that small
changes over vast time add up to new

2
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.740
species.

3
00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:13.170
His book closed with a famous sentence:
there is grandeur in this view of life,

4
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:17.160
first breathed into a
few forms, or into one.

5
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:22.060
A year later, for the second edition,
he added three words to that sentence.

6
00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:26.080
So if science can explain how
the universe and life developed,

7
00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.970
is anything left for a creator to do?

8
00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:33.050
In this mission, you'll follow
natural selection step by step:

9
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.060
variation, inheritance,
struggle and selection.

10
00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:42.340
Then you'll weigh Richard Dawkins' blind
watchmaker against believers' replies.

11
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:46.920
Your mission: weigh up whether science
leaves anything for a creator to do.
